#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186203858 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204085 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "efe27056-c688-56de-9859-98464f57ef64" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Basic Subset Gradients"}] :question/id #uuid "aba1787c-af4b-5adc-8302-6302e891978b" :question/math-academy-id "e-17532" :question/problem "Given the function $f(x,y,z,w) = xyzw,$ compute $\\nabla_{x,w} \\: f.$" :question/worked-solution "To compute $\\nabla_{x,w} \\: f$, we take partial derivatives with respect to $x$ and $w$ only.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=\\frac{∂}{∂x}(xyzw) & =yzw \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂w}=\\frac{∂}{∂w}(xyzw) & =xyz\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∇}_{x,w}\\,f & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂w}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}yzw \\\\ xyz\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186203859 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204086 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c6646d65-7c0f-56ae-995d-1de831893ab9" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Parameter Subset Gradients"}] :question/id #uuid "9599c265-6015-5ad4-b379-d72a67a1a475" :question/math-academy-id "e-17533" :question/problem "Given the function ![](images/df/dfff3e067517ee22189d8854be536b1c8955fb428ac7a7fc2297784243c058be.svg), compute ![](images/ce/ce5740fe7feadf98e660316bbe3d70877c382a03ae14748acfb749afa534aacf.svg)" :question/worked-solution "To compute ![](images/eb/eba21b079adea46f7772d028bf4d6371aa9afb7fa47bbc85b6c4a99a0bb2fe26.svg), we take partial derivatives with respect to ![](images/34/349015631ec44ef653936c85586d2c5ef56ba64392b3f92b4b92cbef3e731bc5.svg) and ![](images/a7/a77a353782459b753313d80235712695d65dc4a44d8d357aa41add6729f81d8f.svg).\n\n![](images/1b/1bfde37b8702b599011b80663b78ab27b17685480d50e9e8de578a92faccb880.svg)\n\nTherefore, we obtain the following:\n![](images/15/15bd16ed0589950d568ccb7df71322f094a29760b735f668792668fd322027fb.svg)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186203860 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204088 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "26c6e982-dcf3-5521-84d9-5d8ca8b51a33" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Second-Order Derivatives"}] :question/id #uuid "1639c64c-655b-5822-8464-0f4a704887df" :question/math-academy-id "e-17534" :question/problem "Given the function $f(\\mathbf{x}; \\mathbf{w}) = (w_1x_1 - w_2+x_2)^2,$ compute $\\nabla_{\\mathbf{w}}(\\nabla_{\\mathbf{w}} \\: f).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we compute $\\nabla_{\\mathbf{w}} \\: f$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂{w}_{1}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂{w}_{1}}({w}_{1}{x}_{1}-{w}_{2}+{x}_{2})^{2}=2{x}_{1}({w}_{1}{x}_{1}-{w}_{2}+{x}_{2}) \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂{w}_{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂{w}_{2}}({w}_{1}{x}_{1}-{w}_{2}+{x}_{2})^{2}=-2({w}_{1}{x}_{1}-{w}_{2}+{x}_{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we compute the second derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{w}_{1}^{2}}=2{x}_{1}^{2}\\,\\, &  & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{w}_{1}∂{w}_{2}}=-2{x}_{1} \\\\  & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{w}_{2}∂{w}_{1}}=-2{x}_{1}\\,\\, &  & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{w}_{2}^{2}}=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∇}_{w}({∇}_{w}\\,f) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{w}_{1}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{w}_{1}∂{w}_{2}} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{w}_{2}∂{w}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{w}_{2}^{2}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}^{2} & -2{x}_{1} \\\\ -2{x}_{1} & 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186203863 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204087 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "64331ffc-80a5-50c1-a7ac-d346458ce997" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Vector Subset Gradients"}] :question/id #uuid "91b597c2-12a1-5c93-93fb-dd9dd4a3a9fc" :question/math-academy-id "e-17704" :question/problem "Given the function \n$f(\\mathbf{x}; \\mathbf{w}) = w_1x_1^{3} + w_2x_2^{3},$\ncompute $\\nabla_{\\mathbf{w}} \\: f$ with the input ![](images/35/352c09d0683235e0346b23eb4257530064bb733f3f75f3cfa0ae23cc7d9dde3e.svg)" :question/worked-solution "To compute $\\nabla_{\\mathbf{w}} \\: f$, we take partial derivatives with respect to each component of $\\mathbf{w}.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂{w}_{1}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂{w}_{1}}({w}_{1}{x}_{1}^{3}+{w}_{2}{x}_{2}^{3})={x}_{1}^{3} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂{w}_{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂{w}_{2}}({w}_{1}{x}_{1}^{3}+{w}_{2}{x}_{2}^{3})={x}_{2}^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, with ![](images/ee/ee17ff076572f222a01b38d6527cb22823a721fb5eb6afa33a65f93582b96589.svg) we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∇}_{w}\\,f & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{3} \\\\ {x}_{2}^{3}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}27 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204559 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204085 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "efe27056-c688-56de-9859-98464f57ef64" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Basic Subset Gradients"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "120941c5-b24d-5fee-9a22-d751601b4a4f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2xy" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529613}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "120941c5-b24d-5fee-9a22-d751601b4a4f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2xy" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529613} :answer-field/id #uuid "be30e805-f1c6-5479-9f43-1b97f941cb88" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186203321} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c4c58225-5f24-5dd5-ab65-9e91f60c5343" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+{z}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530071}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c4c58225-5f24-5dd5-ab65-9e91f60c5343" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+{z}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530071} :answer-field/id #uuid "e3f1f724-9806-58ef-aa98-ba6847cbc23c" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186203322}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "90dbed3e-86ce-5b42-be6c-68de8714331b" :question/math-academy-id "q-263486" :question/problem "Given the function $f(x,y,z)={x}^{2}y+y{z}^{2},$ compute ${∇}_{x,y}\\,f.$\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\" rowspan=\"2\" width=\"30px\">${∇}_{x,y}\\,f=\\text{ }$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "To compute ${∇}_{x,y}\\,f$, we take partial derivatives with respect to $x$ and $y$ only.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}y+y{z}^{2}) & =2xy \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y}=\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}y+y{z}^{2}) & ={x}^{2}+{z}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∇}_{x,y}\\,f & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2xy \\\\ {x}^{2}+{z}^{2}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204563 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204088 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "26c6e982-dcf3-5521-84d9-5d8ca8b51a33" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Second-Order Derivatives"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ee3b433a-8aac-53f7-9d1b-048009d1ca9d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x_1x_2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530177}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ee3b433a-8aac-53f7-9d1b-048009d1ca9d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x_1x_2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530177} :answer-field/id #uuid "32c25c87-9230-542f-9e1e-4e04d4a253ab" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186203331} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b210a9de-3fb8-5d18-b918-2389d8cea160" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x_2^2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530026}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b210a9de-3fb8-5d18-b918-2389d8cea160" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x_2^2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530026} :answer-field/id #uuid "7c6796e7-71f5-5e98-9a2e-b52f1df475d0" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186203332}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "42c18789-1e5f-52ac-ac15-9c282210e0f5" :question/math-academy-id "q-263490" :question/problem "Given the function $f(x;w)=({w}_{1}{x}_{1}+{w}_{2}{x}_{2})^{2},$ compute ${∇}_{w}({∇}_{w}\\,f).$\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\" rowspan=\"2\" width=\"30px\">${∇}_{w}({∇}_{w}\\,f)=\\text{ }$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">$2{x}_{1}^{2}$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">$2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "First, we compute ${∇}_{w}\\,f$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂{w}_{1}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂{w}_{1}}({w}_{1}{x}_{1}+{w}_{2}{x}_{2})^{2}=2({w}_{1}{x}_{1}+{w}_{2}{x}_{2}){x}_{1} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂{w}_{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂{w}_{2}}({w}_{1}{x}_{1}+{w}_{2}{x}_{2})^{2}=2({w}_{1}{x}_{1}+{w}_{2}{x}_{2}){x}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we compute the second derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{w}_{1}^{2}}=2{x}_{1}^{2}\\,\\, &  & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{w}_{1}∂{w}_{2}}=2{x}_{1}{x}_{2} \\\\  & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{w}_{2}∂{w}_{1}}=2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}\\,\\, &  & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{w}_{2}^{2}}=2{x}_{2}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∇}_{w}({∇}_{w}\\,f) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{w}_{1}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{w}_{1}∂{w}_{2}} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{w}_{2}∂{w}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{w}_{2}^{2}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}^{2} & 2{x}_{1}{x}_{2} \\\\ 2{x}_{1}{x}_{2} & 2{x}_{2}^{2}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186530443 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204085 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "efe27056-c688-56de-9859-98464f57ef64" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Basic Subset Gradients"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "78cd906e-dc0b-56ce-b0b6-24dfc3eeae85" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "xz e^{xyz}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529888}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "78cd906e-dc0b-56ce-b0b6-24dfc3eeae85" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "xz e^{xyz}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529888} :answer-field/id #uuid "afd5dbcb-74bc-5c07-a182-140a896ce903" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530344} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "db346e62-1def-5a72-9ff0-a38dc40f2ab5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "yz e^{xyz}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530120}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "db346e62-1def-5a72-9ff0-a38dc40f2ab5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "yz e^{xyz}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530120} :answer-field/id #uuid "d0871417-91fa-595c-885a-0195bb317353" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530372}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "30241212-e00e-5866-b2f3-3d6f4d26064b" :question/math-academy-id "q-264810" :question/problem "Given the function $f(x,y,z)={e}^{xyz},$ compute ${∇}_{x,y}\\,f.$\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\" rowspan=\"2\" width=\"30px\">${∇}_{x,y}\\,f=\\text{ }$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">\n{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">\n{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "To compute ${∇}_{x,y}\\,f$, we take partial derivatives with respect to $x$ and $y$ only.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=\\frac{∂}{∂x}({e}^{xyz}) & =yz{e}^{xyz} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y}=\\frac{∂}{∂y}({e}^{xyz}) & =xz{e}^{xyz}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∇}_{x,y}\\,f & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}yz{e}^{xyz} \\\\ xz{e}^{xyz}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186530467 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204085 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "efe27056-c688-56de-9859-98464f57ef64" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Basic Subset Gradients"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #u