∇}_{x,z}\\,f$, we take partial derivatives with respect to $x$ and $z$ only.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x{y}^{3}+{y}^{3}z) & ={y}^{3} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂z}=\\frac{∂}{∂z}(x{y}^{3}+{y}^{3}z) & ={y}^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∇}_{x,z}\\,f & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂z}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{y}^{3} \\\\ {y}^{3}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186530474 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204085 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "efe27056-c688-56de-9859-98464f57ef64" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Basic Subset Gradients"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c1b6661d-a08a-5c9c-97ea-75c8ed8b1a7e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x}{z}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530063}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c1b6661d-a08a-5c9c-97ea-75c8ed8b1a7e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x}{z}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530063} :answer-field/id #uuid "2c1adc0a-c465-5765-a271-6cf456d2ee26" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530252} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c49d497a-5133-5547-a1e5-47527e18b642" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{xy}{{z}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530070}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c49d497a-5133-5547-a1e5-47527e18b642" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{xy}{{z}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530070} :answer-field/id #uuid "8a5606ec-22d8-59ef-accf-8e2b329fb9d3" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 175921